PURPOSE of /kernel/distribution/ltp/generic
Description: Linux Test Project Generic

LTP Introduction
================
LTP is a famous test suite under Linux, I port LTP to Beaker every
4 months (+/-1 month if needed). You can use this testcase for your
RHEL testing.

Parameters
==========
TESTARGS		LTP job file to run, see configs dir in git repo
TEST_VERSION		Running a specific version of LTP other than the default
FILTERTESTS		Running some specific testcases other than the default
			e.g. FILTERTESTS="accept01 readahead01"
SKIPTESTS		Specify test list that not run, seperated by space
			e.g. SKIPTESTS="rename11 rename13"
			useful to disable specific tests temporarily
REPORT_FAILED_RESULT	Report each failed test to beaker if set to "yes"
SKIP_LEVEL		0) - none of the knownissues will be skiped, only change
			     from 'FAIL' to 'KNOW' in test log
			1) - only skip the fatal knownissues, and mark the others
			     from 'FAIL' to 'KNOW' in test log
			     BTW, it'll go to this way if the 'SKIP_LEVEL' not set
			2) - skip all of the knownissues on test system


# Notes: SKIP_LEVEL is different to SKIPTESTS. SKIP_LEVEL is based on a script only
	 to handle the known issues. And SKIPTESTS is used to skip general case in
	 ltp/generic test suit.
OPTS		provide extra parameter to kirk command line
			e.g. OPTS="--suite-timeout 36000"
